WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.968
-Happy Thanksgiving to you.
Nice to see you.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.501
-Thank you so much.
Nice to see you, too.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.400
-Thanks for coming on.
Thanksgiving exciting for you?

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.067
Not exciting? Do you have
a big family gathering?

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.501
-No, not exciting.
Not exciting, no.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.267
-No, not exciting?
-No, no.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:15.334
So, I come from a family of --
of vegetarians and vegans,

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:17.100
and, um -- Yeah, yeah, I mean --

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.667
And, I mean, all due res--
You know.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.367
And, um, yeah.
-Yeah, so --

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.634
-Yeah, so, no, we do, like,
a "Thanks-living,"

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:26.067
which is, you know --
which is, like, a pun.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.033
Which is not fun
in and of itself,

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.234
but also when it applies
to a vegan Thanksgiving.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.200
-Thanks-living.
-Thanks-living. Yeah, so we --

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.467
-What happens at Thanks-living?
-We -- we -- You know,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.701
we buy a turkey, which is
essentially saving a turkey.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:41.033
And we put that picture of the
turkey, you know, on the table,

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.801
instead of turkey food,
you know.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.000
And it says little things like,
you know,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.367
"Oh, it's Bagel, and he likes
to run around and..."

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.734
You know, and stuff like that.

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.968
And so anyway,
then we don't eat turkey,

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:55.968
but we do feel the guilt
of it anyway.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.667
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.267
You see -- You're looking
at Bagel the whole evening.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.567
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.334
-And talking about
how he likes to run around

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.000
and other activities
that a turkey does.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.834
-It gets worse. Yeah.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:10.667
Yeah, no, so, like, my sister
will read from this book,

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.467
"Eating Animals"
by Jonathan Safran Foer.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.000
-Oh, my goodness!

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.801
-I don't know if you've read
this book, but it's basically --

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.200
It takes you through
the factory farming process.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.834
So I'm sitting there
eating asparagus.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:25.200
I've already committed
to what you've wanted. Yeah.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.501
-What foods do you eat
besides asparagus?

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.300
-They make loaves. Loaves.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.767
Everything goes into a loaf.
You have lentil loaf.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:34.701
Loaves.
-Lentil loaf.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.868
-Lentil loaf.
-Oh. Like a non-meat loaf.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.667
-That's it. Sweet potato loaf.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:41.767
Anything that you probably
don't want to eat,

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.033
they turn into a loaf,

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.934
and then we have to sit there
and eat it, yeah.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:48.934
-Loaves-giving, yeah.
Thanks-living. Alright.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.000
Well, that's good.
Do you cook at all?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.701
-No, I don't cook. I don't cook.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.601
Which is probably, you know,
why I wound up going

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.367
to a Thanks-living
every year 'cause --

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.200
I should be taking control
of my life.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.834
You know what I mean?
-Yeah, no, this is good.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.968
I think you'll have
a fun -- a fun time.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.534
I want to talk about
"Fleishman Is in Trouble."

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:04.767
-Yeah.
-Congratulations.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.300
You are Fleishman.
-Yeah. That's right.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.667
That's right.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:14.267
-It's great. It's smart.
It's funny. It's very New York.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.868
You and Claire Danes...
-Yeah.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.901
-...who I love. Have you
ever worked with Claire?

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:21.234
-No, no. I mean, it was amazing.
We -- I did meet her once.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.534
I met her probably,
like, 15 years ago.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.601
I -- She has
no recollection of it,

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.968
which is the impression
I normally make on people.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.167
But especially --
especially in this case.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.767
-When did you meet Claire Danes?

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:34.501
-So, my wife had to go to some
benefit, and I was with her.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.033
And I had to go with her.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.434
And I just got really high
because I --

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.701
I knew it was
going to be boring.

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:41.901
And then --

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:47.601
And I -- I got, you know --
I got separated from her there.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:50.467
You know, and I wound up
talking to this woman.

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:53.601
And she -- We had gone
to the same high school,

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.634
and she said she was an actress,
and she went to Yale.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:56.968
And I was just thinking,
"My God.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:58.334
This is, like,
the coolest person

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:00.901
I've ever met in my life."
And I -- I told her that.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.100
And then, I walked over
to my wife, and I said,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.801
"Honey, I think
I just met my soulmate.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.601
I met this amazing woman."

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:10.801
And I pointed to the woman
who I wanted to be my soulmate,

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.601
and Anna, my wife, she said,

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.534
"That's Claire Danes,
you idiot. Good luck."

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.000
Yeah.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.234
-Were you --
Were you married to your wife?

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.200
-I wasn't married to her,
but things were going well.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.868
-You were dating her
at the time.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:27.200
-I was dating her, yeah.
You know, we did a dry run.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.300
[ Laughter ]
-Now you're happily married.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.734
And all these years later,

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.000
here you are working
with Claire Danes.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.200
-Yeah, but she had
no recollection

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.133
of the greatest day of my life.

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:38.601
-Yeah. [ Laughs ] Oh, my gosh.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.334
For this series,
you told me backstage

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:42.334
that there was something
they asked you to do

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.801
you were a little
apprehensive about.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.200
-Yes, yes.
-Can we talk about it?

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.767
I think it'll be good
to talk about it.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.834
-Yeah. I mean, I'm apprehensive
about most things.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.067
But in particular, they wanted
me to be naked in this.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.701
You know,
they wanted me to be naked.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.334
Not -- Not my front.
You all know what --

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.734
Everybody knows
what the difference is.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.434
-Sure.
-And so -- But my back.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:01.367
And I'm, not, like -- I'm not
a very comfortable person naked.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.868
You know?
-No.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.767
-No, I mean, I would shower
in a bathing suit if it meant,

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.901
you know, staying --
if it wasn't unsanitary.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.400
-Of course. Yeah, of course.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.000
-Just so I don't have to see
anything. You know what I mean?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.200
And I also have, you know,
the same body -- For the last,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.167
really, 30 years,
I've had the same body.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:21.701
And so um -- And, yeah --

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:22.968
But anyway,
they wanted me to be naked.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.234
-So you're not parading around
saying,

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.434
"Hey, this is the way I live."

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:26.801
-I have three more jokes
about my body.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.300
No, yeah, yeah. Sorry.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.334
So, anyway, they wanted me to
be naked, and I was mortified.

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:31.934
You know, and I thought,
"Okay, well let me --"

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.701
They asked me so, so nicely.

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.534
And I thought "Okay,
well let me call my wife,

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:38.100
'cause she'll say no,
and then I can say,
'You know, my wife said no.'"

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.033
So, I called my wife,
and she said,

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.234
"Well, is the woman
in the scene naked?"

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:43.601
And I said, "Yes."

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.801
And she said, "Well, then
obviously you have to be naked."

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.000
I was like, "I was calling you

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.634
'cause I thought
you would say no."

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:50.501
-"You're my excuse out of this."
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.434
Anyway, she --
she had already hung up.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.667
So I --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.567
Anyway, so,
I was naked in the show.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:57.868
I was, you know --
-Wow.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.534
-It was deeply shameful.
-Yeah.

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:03.000
Did it change anything for you?
Did it feel like, "Wow"?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.634
Like you've -- I don't know.

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:07.601
-No, no, I didn't feel like,
oh, I conquered anything.

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:09.400
-Yeah. That's what
I meant to say. Yeah.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.167
-It was more like,
oh, I just did this thing

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:13.033
that I'm embarrassed by,
but then when it comes out,

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:16.200
I'm gonna be doubly embarrassed
by it, you know?

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.167
-At Thanks-living,
do you not bring up the show?

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.133
-You know, I told my parents

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.934
that there was no premiere
in New York.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:26.567
I said, "I think they're just
gonna go to air with this one."

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:28.367
-"They're just gonna go straight
to Hulu on this one," yeah.

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:29.567
-Yeah, "I don't think
you have Hulu."

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.334
And then I'm gonna disable it
on their TV.

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:33.200
-Oh, my gosh.
-They're not going to know.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.834
-Can we set up what "Fleishman
Is in Trouble" is about?

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.234
It's a great novel, by the way.
It's a good read, as well.

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:38.667
-Yes, yes, yes. It's by --

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.901
I guess you're a fan of
Taffy Brodesser-Akner.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.367
The writer. She's a genius.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:45.200
-I love her. She's so great
and funny and smart.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.834
And it's a great book.

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:48.701
-And more importantly,
you're in the show.

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:50.100
You're in
"Fleishman Is in Trouble."

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.267
-I do full frontal nudity
in this.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.701
I didn't want to do it at first,
but I called my wife --

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:57.133
-She was like,
"Is Jesse doing back?"

00:05:57.133 --> 00:05:58.434
-"Is Jesse doing back?"

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:00.234
-"If Jesse does back,
you gotta do front."

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:01.934
-You gotta be fair. Exactly.

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:04.167
-Yeah, you gotta see both sides
of what a man looks like.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:06.434
-Of course, you do, yeah.
I'm not sure if people will

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:08.634
understand when they see
my front, but it's alright.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.000
-Exactly. They'll probably
think it's my back.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.000
But anyway -- No, yeah, so the
show is about this couple --

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.067
-You're saying my front
looks like your back?

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.267
-I'm just -- Yeah.

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:19.767
[ Laughter ]
-That's very funny.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.534
-Oh, thanks.
-That's very, very funny.

00:06:21.534 --> 00:06:23.133
How do we set up the show?
Sorry.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:25.701
-Oh, yeah, the show is,
you know, about this --

00:06:25.701 --> 00:06:27.734
Oh, I'm not -- It's not true.
-No, no, no, it's not.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:29.367
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.033
No, the show is about, like,
a couple divorcing.

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:32.534
They're going through, like,
a bad divorce.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:36.634
And then she drops the kids off
with me and disappears,

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:38.501
and no one knows where she is.

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:39.868
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:41.634
-Alright. I want to show a clip.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.234
Here's Jesse Eisenberg
and Claire Danes

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:47.133
in "Fleishman Is in Trouble."
Take a look at this.

00:06:47.133 --> 00:06:49.267
-No, actually, I'm just
asking a question, Toby.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:50.634
It's an honest question.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:52.300
-Can I get Instagram?
Everyone has it.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.300
-No, we've answered this before.
No social media until you're 13.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.467
-Everyone.

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:58.200
-Hannah, you don't
even have a phone.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.534
It's not good
for kids and anxiety.

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:01.100
Your brain is still developing,
alright?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.634
-Dad and I will talk about it.
-Excuse me.

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:04.000
We've already talked
about it, okay?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.534
-How about my anxiety

00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:07.634
that everybody is always on it
and leaving me out?!

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:09.367
-She has a point.
-Yeah?

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.601
[ Thud, water running ]

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:23.200
-You're an animal.

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:28.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:30.467
Throwing raw chicken.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, raw chicken.

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:31.634
-Jesse Eisenberg, everybody.

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.868
Check out
"Fleishman Is in Trouble."

00:07:33.868 --> 00:07:35.367
It's great. Right now on Hulu.

